branch: feature/optics-outside-demo-routes
worktree: ../okay-wt-demo

why: a STALE COMMENT that became a defect when somebody else's fix
  landed. ChatDemo's `/events/` route says "requestOf keeps the path
  only, a query string never reaches the route (found the hard way)".
  That was true of Jetty until e9901797 (http-request-query,
  2026-09-03), which fixed Jetty silently dropping the query so it now
  carries `path?query` like the JDK and Netty backends always did.
  The comment stayed; the assumption under it did not.

  So every `r.url == "..."` in ChatDemo is open again, and one of them
  is worse than a 404: `/events/board` is matched exactly and
  `/events/` by PREFIX, in that order. With a query string the exact
  match fails, the prefix one takes it, and the caller gets an inbox
  stream for the email "board?x=1" instead of the board feed. Silently
  wrong rather than refused.

what: ChatDemo's routes become a `Router` — which cuts the query
  before matching (stage 3) — so the whole class goes at once. The
  stale comment goes with it.

first: a test that FAILS on master, because this is a fix and the
  repository's rule is to watch it fail first.

next: the failing test, the conversion, the Live suite, docs
